{"type":"thinking","text":"Now I understand the workflow. Key points:\n\n- artifact_dir = lineage dir (fanout lineage override) — the lineage dir itself is the research packet. So state files go directly in `.../dsh-rc3/deep-research-config.json`, `.../deep-research-state.jsonl`, etc. Wait — in fan-out lineage mode, the lineage directory is the artifact_dir. So yes, files go at lineage root.\n- phase_init: create directories (prompts, iterations, deltas), create config, state log via gateway, strategy, registry. Spec mutation steps: step_detect_spec_present and step_preinit_spec_branch write to spec.md — but our write surface is ONLY lineage dir, so we must NOT write spec.md. The dispatch prompt says every file inside lineage dir only. So skip spec.md writes (they'd be out of scope). Record conflict in iteration? Well, we can note that in the synthesis. The dispatch prompt says follow workflow within write limits, record conflict.\n- phase_loop: one iteration, inline. Write iteration-001.md, deltas/iter-001.jsonl, gateway record, then reduce-state.cjs.\n- phase_synthesis: compile research.md (state_paths.research_output = {artifact_dir}/research.md, not inside research/ subdir since artifact_dir is the lineage). Actually in the skill, research_output = \"{artifact_dir}/research.md\". For a normal packet, that's the packet's research.md. Here artifact_dir is lineage dir so `research.md` at root of lineage.\n- step_update_config_status: edit config status complete (inside lineage).\n- step_convergence_report: run synthesis-closeout.cjs with event-dir then gateway each event. This is part of the workflow. Need to check what it does.\n- step_stage_artifact_dir: skip since fanout_lineage_artifact_dir present. Good.\n- phase_save: probably skip (save continuity) — dispatch prompt says run phase_init, phase_main_loop, phase_synthesis. Not phase_save. Good.\n\nThe research topic: \"What do the checked-in route patches under .dsh/patches/ declare for endpoint, model id and reasoning effort? Read the files and answer in under 150 words.\"\n\nSo the main research is simple: read `.dsh/patches/` files.\n\nLet me now read the config template, strategy template, prompt pack iteration template, and check the artifacts needed. Also check the `append-mode-event.cjs`, `reduce-state.cjs`, and `synthesis-closeout.cjs` usage — maybe run --help. But careful with tool call budget; the persona says max 12 tool calls per iteration, but this process is the whole lineage executor, so more is fine. Still, be efficient.\n\nLet me read the templates and prompt pack."}
