hat do the checked-in route patches under .dsh/patches/ declare for endpoint, model id and reasoning effort? Read the files and answer in under 150 words.\" So the answer content must be <150 words. I'll make the \"Findings\" concise and include a 150-word answer. The iteration narrative structure should have Focus, Actions Taken, Findings, Questions Answered, Questions Remaining, Next Focus (prompt pack) plus persona required sections (Ruled Out, Dead Ends, Edge Cases, Sources Consulted, Assessment, Reflection, Recommended Next Focus). I'll include all.\n\n- `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` with iteration record first, then one finding row per finding with sources. Findings count = number of numbered findings. I'll pick 3 findings:\n  1. LLM Gateway route declares endpoint `https://api.llmgateway.io/v1`, model id `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, reasoning effort `max` (with off/high/max options).\n  2. OpenCode Go route declares endpoint `https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1`, model id `deepseek-v4.1-flash`, reasoningEffort `max`; comment says endpoint unverified until keyed run.\n  3. The non-route patches (guards, lineage, mcp-code-mode) declare no endpoint/model/reasoning effort — only plugin/config/telemetry setup, confirming exactly two route patches.\n  Could add compatibility details: both use openai-completions API, thinkingFormat deepseek, supportsDeveloperRole false, apiKeyEnv names. Those are useful. Maybe split:\n  1. llmgateway endpoint/model/effort\n  2. opencode-go endpoint/model/effort\n  3. both route patches share openai-completions + deepseek thinking format, and other patches are not route patches.\n- iteration record: type iteration, iteration 1, run 1, mode research, target_agent deep-research, agent_definition_loaded true, resolved_route, status complete, focus, findingsCount 3, newInfoRatio maybe 1.0 (all findings new). There is a +0.10 simplicity bonus? The topic fully answered. newInfoRatio: fully new 3/3 = 1.0, capped 1.0. Keep 1.0.\n- keyQuestions: from stra