{"type":"thinking","text":"Init done. Now iteration 1.\n\nLet me carefully prepare the iteration narrative. The answer must be <150 words. Let me draft and count.\n\nAnswer draft:\n\"Two checked-in route patches declare the routing contract. `route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` sets endpoint `https://api.llmgateway.io/v1`, model id `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, and `reasoningEffort: max`, with an off/high/max effort ladder. `route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml` sets endpoint `https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1`, model id `deepseek-v4.1-flash`, and `reasoningEffort: max`, same ladder; its header says the endpoint is unverified until a keyed run. Both configure an `openai-completions` provider with DeepSeek thinking format and `supportsDeveloperRole: false`. The other files - `guards.patch.yml`, `lineage.patch.yml`, and `mcp-code-mode.patch.yml` - declare plugins, telemetry/session disables, and an MCP server, so they declare no endpoint, model id, or reasoning effort.\"\n\nCount: let's count roughly. I'll use a shell to count after writing. But I can count now mentally: \nTwo(1) checked-in2 route3 patches4 declare5 the6 routing7 contract8. route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml9 sets10 endpoint11 https://...12, model13 id14 deepseek...15, and16 reasoningEffort17: max18, with19 an20 off/high/max21 effort22 ladder23. route-opencode...24 sets25 endpoint26 url27, model28 id29 id30, and31 reasoningEffort32 max33, same34 ladder35; its36 header37 says38 the39 endpoint40 is41 unverified42 until43 a44 keyed45 run46. Both47 configure48 an49 openai-completions50 provider51 with52 DeepSeek53 thinking54 format55 and56 supportsDeveloperRole57 false58. The59 other60 files61 guards62, lineage63, and64 mcp-code-mode65 declare66 plugins67, telemetry/session68 disables69, and70 an71 MCP72 server73, so74 they75 declare76 no77 endpoint78, model79 id80, or81 reasoning82 effort83.\n\n~83 words plus long tokens count as single words. Under 150. Good. But code identifiers with punctuation count as one word. Fine. Actually the requirement \"in under 150 words\" is satisfied.\n\nIteration file sections:\n- Focus\n- Actions Taken (read-only: listed files, line citations)\n- Findings (3 numbered with SOURCE)\n- Answer (<150 words)\n- Questions Answered (4)\n- Questions Remaining (none)\n- Ruled Out\n- Dead Ends\n- Edge Cases\n- Sources Consulted\n- Assessment\n- Reflection\n- Recommended Next Focus\n\nCitations:\n- llmgateway: endpoint line 9, model line 14, reasoningEffort line 24; reasoning ladder lines 16-19; provider lines 8-12.\n- opencode: endpoint line 10, model line 15, reasoningEffort line 25; unverified comment lines 1-2.\n- guards: line 3 plugin name; lineage lines 5-16; mcp line 4.\n\nFindings:\n1. `llmgateway` route patch pins endpoint, model, effort.\n2. `opencode-go` route patch pins endpoint, model, effort, endpoint unverified.\n3. Remaining patches are not route patches and declare no endpoint/model/effort. (This is a negative finding, still new.)\n\nMaybe a 4th finding on shared provider compatibility (openai-completions, thinkingFormat deepseek, apiKeyEnv names) — that's relevant and supports the answer. But 3 is enough; answer includes compatibility. Keep 3 findings so findingsCount=3 and registry count matches.\n\nRuled out: e.g., \"Treating mcp-code-mode.patch.yml as a route patch — it mounts an MCP server, no provider/model keys.\" and \"Searching outside .dsh/patches/ for route declarations — out of scope; question is scoped to checked-in patches.\"\n\nDead ends: none; all five files readable.\n\nEdge cases: ambiguous input? \"route patches\" could include mcp-code-mode (it configures a server, not a model route); selected narrow interpretation: files named route-*.patch.yml; the rest verified to have no provider/model keys. That's an ambiguity handling. I'll set edgeCase in record to \"ambiguous-input\". Hmm, maybe \"none\" since the filenames make it clear. But documenting the interpretation is good; set edgeCase `ambiguous-input` and explain the selected interpretation. The gateway record accepts arbitrary edgeCase string; reducer may not care.\n\nAssessment: newInfoRatio 1.0, all 3 findings fully new (the lineage started fresh; no prior research on this topic). Questions addressed 4, answered 4.\n\nReflection: what worked (direct read of five small files; line-numbered read); what didn't (no web verification of endpoints, but out of scope/read-only); differently (could grep `baseURL|model:|reasoningEffort` to confirm no hidden declarations in non-route patches; we did read all files fully, so no need).\n\nRecommended next focus: \"None; topic answered. If a follow-up is needed, verify the LLM Gateway and OpenCode Go endpoints with keyed runs (out of this lineage's read-only scope).\" But since max iterations 1, that's fine.\n\nTimestamps: get current. I'll use 2026-11-14T13:21:xx. Let me get time right before writing."}
